{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-09-24T03:43:53.253905+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T21:45:29.013278+00:00", "id": 22929556, "conceptrecid": "22929555", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22929555", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "metadata": {"title": "A four-vertex counterexample to Knudson's persistence-gradient conjecture", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "publication_date": "2026-09-23", "description": "<p>Knudson conjectured that every nonincident persistence pair is joined by exactly one gradient path in the discrete vector field obtained by retaining the incident persistence pairs. This note gives a simplex-wise filtration of a triangulated interval with four vertices and three edges for which one such pair has no gradient path. It disproves Conjecture 2 in Knudson's contribution to Oberwolfach Report 29/2008, p. 1629. The proof consists of three boundary reductions and an inspection of the matching, and the same example works over any field.</p><p>The deposit includes a three-page manuscript, LaTeX source, two exact standard-library Python verifiers, original inputs, and mathematical and priority audit notes. A bounded literature search located no earlier explicit refutation, without guaranteeing historical novelty. This is an unrefereed, AI-assisted preprint; the audits are not external human peer review. Text is CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["persistent homology", "topological data analysis", "computational topology", "discrete Morse theory", "persistence pairing", "persistence-gradient conjecture", "gradient paths", "discrete vector fields", "acyclic matchings", "simplex-wise filtration", "boundary matrix reduction", "zero-dimensional persistence", "Knudson conjecture", "counterexample"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2008/29", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/main/knudson_gradient_path_counterexample", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s00454-002-2885-2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s00454-011-9350-z", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://aleckriebel.github.io/Math/papers/knudson-gradient-path/", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22929555"}}]}}, "title": "A four-vertex counterexample to Knudson's persistence-gradient conjecture", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22929556", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22929556", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22929556?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22929556", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22929556/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22929555", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22929555", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22929555", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22929555", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22929556/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22929556/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22929556/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22929556/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22929556:paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22929556:paper.pdf/